[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218318750","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106442#issuecomment-3218318750","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106442","id":3218318750,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_06We","user":{"login":"bobsayshilol","id":4732955,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MzI5NTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4732955?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bobsayshilol","html_url":"https://github.com/bobsayshilol","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bobsayshilol/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bobsayshilol/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bobsayshilol/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bobsayshilol/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bobsayshilol/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bobsayshilol/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bobsayshilol/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bobsayshilol/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bobsayshilol/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-24T19:21:05Z","updated_at":"2025-08-24T19:21:05Z","body":"This happens for me too:\n\n> Godot v4.4.1.stable (49a5bc7b6) - Fedora Linux 42 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors\n\nBisecting with `--first-parent` reveals that it was introduced by a11364d1e65c5d39996812f1fc3d78823476d376. It looks like moving the game window sends move+resize events to the X server rather than a click-and-drag, so any compositor effects (like wobbly windows in KWin) don't get applied because it's instantaneously teleporting+resizing. As a workaround, commenting out `case FEATURE_WINDOW_EMBEDDING:` in `display_server_x11.cpp` \"fixes\" the issue (by using the old approach instead).\n\nI don't know enough about X11 to offer a fix, but in an attempt at adding a drag event I found that if the editor crashes (or hangs and you manually kill it) then the embedded process will stick around on screen, but since it doesn't have a real window you can't move or close it. Previously this wasn't an issue since the game process had its own window that showed up in the task bar and had a close button, but with the embedded approach the game window is now a fake one owned by the editor that goes away if it dies. You can repro this by hitting play and then forcefully killing the editor process.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218318750/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4147949416","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106442#issuecomment-4147949416","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106442","id":4147949416,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc73PK9o","user":{"login":"shadowmelds","id":25096408,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MDk2NDA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25096408?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shadowmelds","html_url":"https://github.com/shadowmelds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shadowmelds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shadowmelds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shadowmelds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shadowmelds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shadowmelds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shadowmelds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shadowmelds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shadowmelds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shadowmelds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-28T12:00:16Z","updated_at":"2026-03-28T13:02:34Z","body":"<img width=\"3840\" height=\"2160\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1be3013c-495b-4f7e-a451-2880306f341e\" />\n\nI encountered this issue on Niri WM, and it seems the only thing I can do to prevent it is to disable the multi-window option.\n\n---\n\nEnable Edit Settings：run/platforms/linuxbsd/prefer_wayland fix this ！","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4147949416/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":3},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]